-- check/bad: a field access whose field EXISTS but has another type than the
-- one the code needs says so: the record has a `count` field, an `Int`, and
-- `f` returns it as a `String`; `g` reads the same field of an extensible
-- record. The message names the field and shows its type against the needed
-- one, never "This is not a record with a `count` field".
f : { count : Int } → String
f x = x.count


g : { r | count : Int } → String
g x = x.count
